  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $\\alpha, \\beta$ be the roots of the equation.\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\alpha+\\beta=a-2$ and $\\alpha \\beta=-(a+1)$\r\n\r\nNow, $\\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}=(\\alpha+\\beta)^{2}-2 \\alpha \\beta$\r\n\r\n$=(a-2)^{2}+2(a+1)=(a-1)^{2}+5$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}$ will be minimum if $(a-1)^{2}=0$,\r\n\r\ni.e. $a=1$.",
    "image": null
